# Packages-Root — the allow-list for Runink River, the developer workstation (KDE Plasma on
# Wayland, s6, encrypted ZFS root, one pinned kernel).
#
# artools installs profile.yaml's rootfs lists on top of its own desktop common.yaml; every
# package profile.yaml names must be listed here (river lint profile-manifest), and the
# closure of this list is checked against forbidden.closure (river lint closure).
#
# NOT on this image, deliberately: a Kubernetes node, NAT64, platform runtimes, model
# payloads. A downstream distribution that needs them builds its own profile from this
# repository's packaging (docs/BUILD.md, "Downstream distributions").

# ── base + boot ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
base
linux-runink

mkinitcpio
grub
efibootmgr

# ── firmware ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A workstation fleet is not one SKU: the reference machine is AMD (Radeon, HawkPoint), and
# amdgpu will not initialise without its firmware split. Both vendors are listed so one image
# boots either.
linux-firmware-amdgpu
linux-firmware-intel

# ── ZFS root ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Encrypted ZFS root (invariant 3); the datasets are created with compression=zstd by the
# installer.
runink-zfs
runink-zfs-utils

# ── installer ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# From the pinned [runink] local repo: river-hwprobe + river-plan (the
# install plan runink-install confirms by disk serial) and river-netsetup + river-netcheck
# (the network-first step the live session opens with).
runink-installer
# Live-medium boot and the installer's disk tools (the installed machine is a clone of the live
# rootfs, so they stay on it too).
squashfs-tools
# NOT mkinitcpio-nfs-utils (removed 2026-10-01). It ships `ipconfig` and `nfsmount` for
# mkinitcpio's `net` hook — NFS-root boot — and no initramfs this image builds names that
# hook: the live one comes from iso-initcpio's /etc/mkinitcpio-default.conf
# (base udev artix_shutdown artix artix_loop_mnt artix_kms modconf block filesystems
# keyboard keymap), the installed one from root-overlay/etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/zfs.conf.
# Nothing in the resolved closure requires it, nothing in this repository referenced it, and
# docs/OWN-BASE.md already listed it as a drop.
artools-base
dialog
parted
gptfdisk
dosfstools

# ── s6 init ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# s6, NOT systemd. This is a hard invariant of the image and it constrains the desktop:
# every service below must have an s6 counterpart, which is why the -s6 packages are named
# explicitly rather than relying on a plasma meta-package to drag in systemd units.
s6
s6-rc
s6-linux-init
s6-scripts
elogind-s6
dbus-s6
networkmanager-s6
openssh-s6
# bluez-s6 ships the `bluetoothd` s6-rc bundle (bluetoothd-srv + bluetoothd-log, depends on
# dbus); cups-s6 ships `cupsd`. Both are enabled in profile.yaml's live-session.services the
# same way sddm is, and 20-clone-rootfs.sh carries the live default bundle to the target.
bluez-s6
cups-s6

# ── network ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
networkmanager
wpa_supplicant
openssh
iptables
nftables

# ── desktop: KDE Plasma on Wayland ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXPLICIT list, not plasma-meta (owner decision 2026-09-24: minimal tech, no telemetry,
# no app store). This is plasma-meta 6.7.5's dependency list MINUS:
#   discover, flatpak-kcm  - app store + Flatpak; the workstation updates by pacman.
#                            flatpak, discover, flatpak-kcm and packagekit are on
#                            forbidden.closure so they cannot come back transitively.
#   plasma-welcome         - first-run wizard (also hard-depends on kuserfeedback)
#   krdp                   - RDP server (freerdp); nothing here should listen for desktops
#   plasma-vault           - gocryptfs/FUSE vaults; the ZFS pool is already encrypted
#   plasma-firewall        - ufw/firewalld KCM; neither backend ships (nftables is used)
#   oxygen, oxygen-sounds  - legacy theme; Breeze is the theme
#   kdeplasma-addons       - REMOVED 2026-10-01. Extra plasmoids (timer, comic, fuzzy clock,
#                            fifteen puzzle, weather, media frame, ...), a few KRunner
#                            plugins (unit converter, dictionary, characters) and the
#                            picture-of-the-day wallpaper plugin. The default desktop here
#                            loads none of them: the River look-and-feel layout
#                            (root-overlay/usr/share/plasma/look-and-feel/
#                            org.runink.river.desktop) uses only
#                            org.kde.plasma.desktop.defaultPanel and
#                            org.kde.plasma.kickoff, both from plasma-desktop/
#                            plasma-workspace. Its only reverse dependency is plasma-meta,
#                            which this image does not install, so it is a leaf — and it is
#                            the ONLY reason qt6-quick3d, openxr (a VR runtime loader),
#                            qt6-quicktimeline and jsoncpp were in the closure at all.
#                            Measured with pactree: 51.7 MiB over 5 packages. What a user
#                            loses: those widgets, in "Add Widgets". KDE's own KRunner
#                            calculator (in krunner/plasma-workspace) stays.
# PLUS sddm-kcm (login-screen settings). konsole and spectacle are listed below.
# kuserfeedback CANNOT be dropped: plasma-workspace, dolphin and kate hard-depend on it
# (pacman -Si, Artix 2026-09-24). It is KDE's opt-in feedback library, off by default
# (nothing is sent unless a user enables it in System Settings), so it stays, and is
# deliberately NOT on forbidden.closure.
aurorae
bluedevil
breeze
breeze-gtk
kactivitymanagerd
kde-cli-tools
kde-gtk-config
kdecoration
kglobalacceld
kinfocenter
kmenuedit
knighttime
kpipewire
kscreen
kscreenlocker
ksshaskpass
ksystemstats
kwallet-pam
kwayland
kwin
kwrited
layer-shell-qt
libkscreen
libksysguard
libplasma
milou
ocean-sound-theme
plasma-activities
plasma-activities-stats
plasma-browser-integration
plasma-desktop
plasma-disks
plasma-integration
plasma-keyboard
plasma-nm
plasma-pa
plasma-systemmonitor
plasma-thunderbolt
plasma-workspace
polkit-kde-agent
powerdevil
print-manager
systemsettings
xdg-desktop-portal-kde
sddm-kcm
sddm
sddm-s6
konsole
dolphin
kate

# ── KDE applications (daily desktop) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Video is `dragon` (KDE's own ffmpeg-based
# player): haruna is NOT in the Artix repos (only Arch [extra]), and this builder is
# Artix-only. okular pulls phonon-qt6 -> phonon-qt6-vlc (the only Phonon backend in
# Artix), which accounts for the vlc-plugin-* entries in the closure.
# partitionmanager (+ kpmcore) adds nothing forbidden; measured 2026-09-24.
dragon
elisa
gwenview
okular
ark
spectacle
kcalc
partitionmanager

# Browser. Its telemetry, studies and default-browser nag are switched off system-wide by
# root-overlay/etc/firefox/policies/policies.json (Mozilla enterprise policies).
firefox

# NOT plasma-workspace-wallpapers — KDE's official wallpaper collection, REMOVED 2026-10-01.
# 255.1 MiB for exactly one package, and this image already ships its own: the default is
# RIVER (branding/wallpapers/River, set by look-and-feel org.runink.river.desktop's
# `Image=River`), the login screen is the `runink-river` SDDM theme
# (root-overlay/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-river.conf), and the fourteen CachyOS Emerald JPEGs are
# vendored under branding/wallpapers/emerald and shipped by branding/render.sh. Nothing in
# the resolved closure depends on it (pactree -r: nothing) and nothing in this repository
# names a wallpaper from it. What a user loses: KDE's stock wallpapers in the picker.
# TO BOOT-TEST: Plasma's compiled-in fallback wallpaper is "Next", which lived in this
# package — confirm the desktop, the lock screen and SDDM all show the River artwork and not
# a flat colour.

# ── boot splash: Plymouth (workstation ONLY) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The RIVER `river` script theme (root-overlay/usr/share/plymouth/themes/river). Artix
# ships plymouth in [world] and its mkinitcpio hook has a non-systemd path (add_runscript;
# the busybox hook starts plymouthd), so it is s6-clean. Its dependencies (cairo, pango,
# fontconfig, freetype2, libx11, libdrm, libxkbcommon, xkeyboard-config, glib2) are
# already in this closure: measured with pactree (2026-09-22), plymouth adds only itself
# (the s6/Artix subtrees are unresolvable off-box; recheck on Artix).
# s6 has no plymouth-quit.service; root-overlay/etc/s6/adminsv/plymouth-quit does that job.
plymouth

# ── graphics: mesa ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vulkan-radeon for the AMD reference machine, vulkan-intel so the same image is usable on
# Intel hardware. libva for hardware video decode.
mesa
vulkan-icd-loader
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
libva-mesa-driver
mesa-utils

# ── multimedia: codecs + hardware video ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# GStreamer (what Plasma/KDE apps and Firefox's WebRTC use) plus ffmpeg (dragon, Qt
# Multimedia). intel-media-driver is the Meteor Lake (iHD) VA-API driver; the AMD
# reference machine decodes through libva-mesa-driver above. libva-utils gives vainfo.
gst-plugins-base
gst-plugins-good
gst-plugins-bad
gst-plugins-ugly
gst-libav
ffmpeg
intel-media-driver
libva-utils

# ── audio ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-alsa
wireplumber
# JACK clients through PipeWire (pro-audio apps without a separate jack2 server). The
# volume UI is plasma-pa, in the Plasma list above, so pavucontrol-qt is not added.
pipewire-jack

# ── bluetooth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bluedevil (the Plasma applet) is in the Plasma list above; this is the stack under it. The
# s6 service (bluez-s6) is with the other -s6 packages above.
bluez
bluez-utils

# ── printing ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# print-manager (the Plasma printer KCM) is in the Plasma list above and is
# useless without a CUPS daemon. system-config-printer is deliberately NOT added: it
# duplicates print-manager and drags in python-gobject/gtk3 bindings.
cups

# ── fonts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ttf-dejavu
ttf-liberation
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
noto-fonts-cjk
# NOT noto-fonts-extra (removed 2026-10-01). 331.3 MiB for one package, and it adds no
# SCRIPT this image could not already render: measured against the Artix file database, all
# 84 font families in noto-fonts-extra are among the 226 in noto-fonts, and what it adds is
# extra WIDTHS and WEIGHTS of them (Condensed / SemiCondensed / ExtraCondensed, and a couple
# of Semibold faces). noto-fonts, noto-fonts-cjk and noto-fonts-emoji keep the coverage.
# Nothing in the resolved closure depends on it. What a user loses: those width and weight
# variants in a font picker.

# ── developer toolchain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A developer workstation clones and builds: base-devel, git and curl are its tools (invariant
# 5 is written for this; see AGENTS.md).
base-devel
git
curl
rsync
vim
# The terminal greeting: fish (the users' login shell) and fastfetch (the machine summary).
fish
fastfetch
sudo
go
zstd

# ── compression + power ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# zram is configured by the s6 service in root-overlay (zram-generator is a systemd
# generator and cannot be used here). util-linux provides zramctl.
util-linux
cpupower

# ── sandbox ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# bubblewrap: unprivileged (not setuid) and adds only itself to the closure. river-sandbox
# (root-overlay/usr/local/bin) runs untrusted code under it (invariant 8).
bubblewrap
